>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `[arith_split]`

``` hol4
Theorem theorem_name[arith_split]:
  split_rule
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers a persistent operator-splitting rule for full linarith tactics.

The argument-free `[arith_split]` theorem attribute accepts a split in
P-form, usually
`!P ... . P (operator arguments) <=> branch_formula`. Both conclusion and
assumption forms are accepted. Declarations are shape-validated, inherited
through theory ancestry, and used by
`LINARITH_TAC` and `CFG_LINARITH_TAC`. They are not used by
`SIMPLE_LINARITH_TAC`, the forward prover, reducer, or simplifier solver.

This set is distinct from the simplifier's `[split]` attribute. The
per-invocation counterpart is `markerLib.Split th` (also available as
`simpLib.Split th`). The persistent attribute is named `[arith_split]`,
not `[linarith_split]`. Use `linarithData.remove_arith_split` for
persistent removal.

### Failure

The attribute takes no arguments and rejects theorems that do not have the
required P-form. A full tactic call can also fail if repeated splitting
exceeds its configured limit.

### Example

``` hol4
Definition choose_num_def:
  choose_num b (x : num) y = if b then x else y
End

Theorem choose_num_split[arith_split]:
  !P b x y.
    P (choose_num b x y) <=>
    (b ==> P x) /\ (~b ==> P y)
Proof
  rw [choose_num_def]
QED

Theorem arith_split_attribute_example:
  !b x y z.
    x <= z /\ y <= z ==> choose_num b x y <= z
Proof
  rpt strip_tac >>
  linarithLib.LINARITH_TAC []
QED
```

